-- title:
--   Exactly q local cosets for the prime Hecke set at q
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b$ be rationals and $q'$ a prime such that $\mathbb{H}=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ is definite and ramified exactly at $q'$, in the sense that $a<0$, $b<0$ and, for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, the completion $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ has all nonzero elements invertible precisely when $q'\in v$. Let $R\subseteq\mathbb{H}$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule which is an Eichler order of level $N$, i.e. $R=\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_2$ for maximal orders $\Lambda_1,\Lambda_2$ with relative index $N$ of $R$ in $\Lambda_1$, and let $q$ be a prime with $q\neq q'$ and $q\nmid N$. Let $n$ be a unit of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},f}$ lying in the prime Hecke set of $R$ at $q$: $n$ and $q\cdot n^{-1}$ lie in the finite adelic box $\widehat{R}$ of $R$, while $n^{-1}\notin\widehat R$ and $q^{-1}\cdot n\notin\widehat R$. Let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ containing $q$. Write $R_v$, $R'_v$ and $S_v$ for the local boxes at $v$ of $R$, of the conjugate $\mathrm{conjByFiniteIdele}\,R\,n$ and of the meet order $\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R\,n=R\cap\mathrm{conjByFiniteIdele}\,R\,n$, these being the additive subgroups of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ generated by $z\otimes c$ with $z$ in the respective lattice and $c$ a $v$-adic integer. Then the set of classes $c$ in the quotient of $(\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v)^{\times}$ by the stabiliser of $S_v$ under the pointwise left multiplication action, for which there exists a unit $g$ with $g\in S_v$, $q\cdot g^{-1}\in S_v$, $g^{-1}\notin S_v$, $q^{-1}\cdot g\notin S_v$, with $g^{-1}xg\in R'_v\iff x\in R_v$ for all $x$, with the analogous equivalence $g^{-1}xg\in R_v\iff x\in R'_v$ failing for some $x$, and with class equal to $c$, has cardinality exactly $q$.
--
--   This is the local count at the place above $q$ underlying the degree of the $U_q$-Hecke correspondence on the class-set graph attached to an Eichler order: the local form at $v$ of the Hecke double coset breaks into exactly $q$ cosets modulo the unit group of the local meet order, an Iwahori subgroup of the split algebra $\mathbb{H}\otimes\mathbb{Q}_v\cong M_2(\mathbb{Q}_v)$. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.ncard_setOf_exists_mem_uHeckeSet_quotientMk_eq_of_mem_primeHeckeSet`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.ncard_setOf_exists_mem_uHeckeSet_quotientMk_eq_of_mem_primeHeckeSet), which transfers the count from the local to the adelic setting.
